Additional Exclusions (applicable only to the Maternity Benefit Endorsement) The insurance under this insuring agreement does not cover the following expenses:
1. any treatments that are not related to childbirth, except for necessary medical treatments to save
the life of the mother or the unborn child(ren);
2. sterilizations, sterilization reversals, contraception, fertility treatments, treatments for newborns;
3. inoculation or vaccination for disease prevention;
4. requests for hospitalization or surgery without being recommended by a physician or surgeon,
including medical services that are not essential to the treatments;
5. medications, treatments, or diagnosis that are not related to the diagnosis, symptoms or conditions
specified in the medical certificate;
6. non-conventional medical treatments including alternative treatments, such as acupuncture,
naturopathy, treatment by massage and acupressure, chiropractic, etc.
7. services by special nurses;
8. all types of prosthetic organs, except artificial heart valves, artificial skull, artificial hip and knee
joints.
Other conditions of the insurance contract and other exclusions are in accordance with this insurance
policy.

Submission of evidence of claim
2.1 Claim for death benefit
The beneficiary(ies) must, at their own expense, submit the following evidence to the company
within 30 days from the date of a covered person's death:
1) benefit claim form prescribed by the company;
2) death certificate;
3) a copy of the autopsy report, certified by a police officer in charge or an authority issuing
the report;
4) a copy of the police daily report/record, certified by a police officer in charge;
5) a copy of the national identification card and copy of the household registration indicating
the "deceased" status of the covered person;
6) a copy of the national identification card and copy of the household registration of the
beneficiary(ies). 7) other documents requested by the company as necessary (if any).

